\description{
Each function takes one table as it arrives and returns it in the shape the search expects, together with a summary of what was dropped and why. Nothing is discarded silently: a row without a date, a code in a system the definitions do not use or a repeated identifier is counted and reported.
}
\details{
A code is compared only within its own coding system. Hierarchical systems (ICD, ICPC, ATC) are compared by prefix, because truncating a code is how a definition says "the whole category"; flat identifiers (SNOMED, RxNorm) are compared whole, since a shorter one is not a parent but a different concept.
